==Latin==

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*ḱens-}}
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*kensēō}}, from {{inh|la|ine-pro||*ḱenséh₁-ye-ti}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*ḱens-||to announce}}. Cognate with {{cog|sa|शंसति|tr=śáṃsati||to declare}}, {{cog|ira-pro|*cánhati}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|cēnseō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|2.p3inf|cēnseō|cēnsu|cēns}}

# to give an [[opinion]]
# to [[think]], [[suppose]] or [[judge]]
#: {{syn|la|credo|reor|opinor|iūdicō|sentio|existimo|cogito|considero|arbitror|puto|reputo}}
# to [[recommend]], [[advise]]
#: {{syn|la|suādeō|commendō|conciliō|dēlīberō|moneō|admoneō|praedicō}}
#* {{Q|la|[[w:Cato the Elder|Cato the Elder]]|quote=[[w:Carthago delenda est|Ceterum '''censeo''' Carthaginem esse delendam]]|t=Furthermore, I '''recommend''' that Carthage must be destroyed}}
# to [[decree]], [[vote]] or [[determine]]
#: {{syn|la|cōnscīscō}}
# to [[count]] or [[reckon]], [[assess]]
# to [[register]] the [[citizens]], [[perform]] the task of a [[censor]]

